From: Cartouche Wine
Subject: [PATCH] wined3d: Recent NVIDIA driver version, RTX 50 cards and a
 VideoDriverVersion setting.

Applies to sources/wine of crossover-sources-26.3.0.tar.gz (SHA-256
ac99c8ca4b3848f3e81784135f023df266b61c2345726ea55a50b3e030dd6872, Wine 11.0).

Games read the display driver version through the D3D9 adapter identifier
(and DXGI's CheckInterfaceSupport, D3D8, DirectDraw), all fed by
wined3d_driver_info_init(). Its newest NVIDIA entry is 531.18
(31.0.15.3118), and Source 2 games such as Deadlock log "old driver" for it.

- DRIVER_NVIDIA_TURING: NVIDIA 581.57 (Game Ready, 2025-10-14), whose
  Windows version is 32.0.15.8157 (the last digit of the third word and the
  fourth word give the public number). Used by the Turing and newer entries
  (GTX 16, RTX 20 to 50, Tesla T4, A10). Older cards keep 531.18.
- RTX 50 cards, device IDs from the PCI ID database
  (https://pci-ids.ucw.cz/read/PC/10de, pci.ids version 2026.10.30):
  2b85 GB202 [GeForce RTX 5090], 2c02 GB203 [GeForce RTX 5080],
  2c05 GB203 [GeForce RTX 5070 Ti], 2f04 GB205 [GeForce RTX 5070].
  Memory is the smallest board's: 32, 16, 16 and 12 GB.
- VideoDriverVersion, a string a.b.c.d read like VideoPciDeviceID (registry
  HKCU\Software\Wine\Direct3D, the per-application key, or WINE_D3D_CONFIG),
  replaces the reported version for any vendor, e.g. 32.0.15.8157.

